Date: Thu, 11 Dec 2025 11:31:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 272/468] PHYTIUM: net: phytmac: fix illegal GFP flags
 combination causing kernel BUG

The driver was using both GFP_DMA and __GFP_DMA32 flags simultaneously,
which is illegal in the ARM64 memory allocation subsystem. This caused
a kernel BUG at include/linux/gfp.h:136 when the VM_BUG_ON() check in
gfp_zone() detected the invalid flag combination.

The issue manifested as:

